<!--
  gradlew checkDev checkSetup checkEntrypoint checkRestore checkPipeSafety

  All five shell suites in one run: the reset guard, the installer's checks, the Minecraft
  entrypoint, the restore guards and the pipefail scan.

  NONE OF THEM NEEDS DOCKER OR A NETWORK - that is the point of them. They drive the scripts'
  functions directly, which is why they can hang off `check` at all.

  They shell out to `bash` off PATH, so they need the same bash 4+ as everything else here; see
  the interpreter note in .run/README.md.

  Why these are Gradle configurations while the `dev:` folders are shell ones - and what the
  interpreter note means - is in .run/README.md.
-->
